  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The scholarly article titled \"Archetypometrics, a Pragmateia: Empirical Determination of the Fundamental Archetypes of Fictional Characters,\" published in 2025, has garnered notable interest, evidenced by 3,232 downloads and a rising count of citations. The research explores the fundamental archetypes in storytelling through a data-driven approach, indicating its initial uptake within scholarly circles.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">At the forefront of contemporary narrative analysis, \"Archetypometrics, a Pragmateia\" investigates the core archetypes that define fictional characters, integrating concepts from literature, sociology, and computer science. Authored by a team from the University of Vermont and the University of California, Berkeley, this work presents a systematic methodology for determining archetypes, contributing a novel perspective to the field of storytelling.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Since its release, the article has registered a total of 1,059 views alongside its impressive download count of 3,232, suggesting significant engagement from the academic community and other stakeholders interested in the dynamics of narrative structure. The early signal of scholarly uptake is reflected in its citation count of one, indicating initial recognition and potential influence within related research disciplines.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Furthermore, the article has demonstrated downstream impact, with one documented instance of reuse, illustrating its relevance and applicability in ongoing studies. The research not only enriches our understanding of archetypal theory but also underlines the interdisciplinary nature of storytelling analysis, fostering connections between philosophy, psychology, and computational approaches.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, \"Archetypometrics\" marks a significant contribution to narrative studies, offering empirical foundations that can lead to deeper insights into character development and storytelling frameworks. As it continues to gain visibility, the work may inspire further research on the intricate relationships between archetypes and audience engagement in narrative forms.</p>",
  "narrative_source": "template"
